// # oodar — Gen 1 Host Substrate (v4.0.0)
//
// Logline: The canonical home of the openOODA Gen 1 host substrate. Compiled openOODA binaries link against the oo_* symbols exported from the 6 per-domain subdirs (core, sec, fs, net, hw, app); the build entry point is `gcc oodar.c`. The umbrella TU is 95 .c files; the public ABI is oodar.h (and the shared type defs in types.h) at the root.
//
// Setup: Pure structural file. The 6 per-domain tactical subdirs mirror std's vocabulary (core, sec, fs, net, hw, app). Each tactical subdir has its own ANCHOR.oo. Some tactical subdirs have nested sub-subdirs (e.g., core/event/, sec/cap/, app/actor/) that also have their own ANCHOR.oo, mirroring std's per-domain organization. The umbrella oodar.c is the single-TU build entry — it #include's the 90 .c files in dependency order. The public API is oodar.h (and the shared type defs in types.h) at the root. The qa/ subdir holds the test utilities and tier-5 tests_challenger_*.c files; they are excluded from the umbrella TU and are not part of the public ABI. The scripts/ subdir holds the Makefile (liboodar.a) and the reproducible-build script (repro_build.sh).
//
// Beats (read in this order):
//   1. types.h          — shared type defs (OoStr, OoIList, OoRes*, OoLL*, OoControlBlock, OoWeakRef, OoPathCap, ...).
//   2. oodar.h          — the public API surface.
//   3. oodar.c          — the umbrella TU (the canonical single-TU build entry).
